In short: you may put the Tride players in your websites and apps, free of charge, including
commercial ones. You may not sell or hand out the players on their own.

Definitions
- "Licensor": Tride Labs Ltd, a company registered in England and Wales, company number 17546581,
  registered office 124 City Road, London, EC1V 2NX, and anyone to whom it transfers the rights in the
  Players (clause 10).
- "Players": the release this licence accompanies — the Tride web player, the Tride iOS and Android
  libraries, the runtime binaries inside them, their source files, documentation, sample code and
  sample scenes. The Tride Editor is not part of the Players; the Tride Terms of Use cover it.
- "You": any person or organisation that receives the Players under this licence, together with
  their employees and contractors while working on Your Products.
- "Your Product": a website, application or other product made by You that plays scenes with the
  Players and does more than only distribute the Players.
- "Your Content": scenes and other material You create, including with the Tride Editor, other than
  the sample scenes.

1. Grant. The Licensor grants You the right to use and copy the Players; to integrate them into Your
   Products; to modify their source files and the sample scenes for that purpose; and to distribute
   the Players, changed or not, as part of Your Products to their users, who may use them as part of
   Your Products. You may do this for any purpose, including commercial ones, without paying the
   Licensor.
   For clarity, all of the following is within this grant and is not a breach of clause 3(a):
   (a) Open-source products. Your Product may be open source: its other parts may come under any
       licences, and this licence puts no condition on them. The Players in it stay under this
       licence; no licence of Your Product applies to them.
   (b) Everyone who gets a copy. Whoever receives the Players, from the Licensor or inside Your
       Product, receives them under this licence and is "You" for products of their own, changed
       versions of Your Product included. As far as this licence is concerned, they may also pass
       Your Product on unchanged, with the Players in it.
   (c) Downloading. Build scripts, package manifests and instructions of Your Product, public ones
       included, may download the Players from where the Licensor publishes them, or tell others
       to do so.
   (d) Source repositories. The source repository of Your Product, a public one included, may hold
       the Players' files, unchanged, as part of Your Product's source, if they stay together with
       this licence and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES, the repository says that the Players are under this
       licence and not under the repository's own, and the repository is not offered as a place to
       get the Players.
2. Duration. The grant in clause 1 is non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free and perpetual for every
   release of the Players You have received under this licence, except as set out in clause 8. Later
   releases may come under different terms; the terms of a release You already have never change.
3. Limits. You may not: (a) sell, license, lend, publish or otherwise make the Players available on
   their own, or as a library, development kit or service for others to build with, other than as
   part of Your Products; (b) attempt to derive source code from the runtime binaries, except where
   the law allows it regardless of this licence; (c) remove copyright or licence notices.
4. Your Content. You own Your Content. This licence gives the Licensor no rights in it. You may
   publish the scene files that are Your Content and license them to anyone on any terms You
   choose, public repositories included; You need no licence from the Licensor for that. The
   Licensor claims no rights in what the Tride Editor generates into those files, such as compiled
   materials. Material of other people inside a scene, such as a font, stays under its own terms.
5. Your changes. Changes, fixes and ideas You send to the Licensor may be used, modified and
   relicensed by the Licensor under any terms, without payment to You. Changes You keep to Yourself
   stay Yours.
6. Name. You may state truthfully that Your Product uses Tride. This licence gives no other right to
   use the name or logo "Tride", and no right to suggest that the Licensor endorses Your Product.
7. Third-party components. The Players contain components under their own licences, listed in
   THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES. Those licences govern those components; nothing here limits them.
8. Termination for breach. If You breach clause 3 and do not cure the breach within 30 days of
   written notice from the Licensor, this licence ends for You. Copies of the Players inside products
   already delivered to their users may remain there.
9. No warranty; liability. The Players are provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. To the
   maximum extent permitted by law, the Licensor is not liable for any loss or damage arising from
